      "stdout": "Done.\n\nI repaired the migration package in the accessible workspace mirror:\n- /workspace/in/billingdb/migration.sql\n- /workspace/in/billingdb/preflight_report.md\n- /workspace/in/billingdb/rollback.sql\n- /workspace/in/billingdb/postcheck.sql\n- /workspace/in/billingdb/migration_report.md\n\nImportant environment note:\n- The exact <HOME>/... path from your prompt is not mounted here.\n- /Users is read-only in this Linux environment, so I could not write there.\n- The matching editable project content was present at /workspace/in/billingdb, and that is where I applied the repair.\n\nWhat changed\n- migration.sql now:\n  - runs inside an explicit transaction\n  - creates payment_orphans if needed\n  - moves orphan payments there before enforcing referential integrity\n  - preserves orphan p4\n  - preserves all invoices and valid payments\n  - preserves invoice created_at values\n  - adds invoices.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'\n  - rebuilds payments with a foreign key to invoices(id)\n  - restores PRAGMA foreign_keys to ON after commit\n  - is safe to rerun without duplicating moved orphans or corrupting counts\n\n- rollback.sql now:\n  - restores old table shapes:\n    - invoices(id, customer_id, total_cents, created_at)\n    - payments(id, invoice_id, amount_cents, created_at)\n  - merges payment_orphans back into payments\n  - drops payment_orphans\n  - runs in an explicit transaction\n\n- postcheck.sql now checks:\n  - row counts\n  - orphan preservation\n  - status null/default expectations\n  - created_at preservation\n  - missing invoice references in payments\n  - foreign key integrity\n\n- preflight_report.md documents:\n  - initial row counts\n  - orphan inventory\n  - required migration actions\n\n- migration_report.md documents:\n  - fixes made\n  - validation results\n  - environment/path caveat\n\nValidation I actually ran\nUsing Python’s built-in sqlite3 (SQLite 3.40.1), I verified:\n- after migration:\n  - invoices = 3\n  - payments = 3\n  - payment_orphans = 1\n  - p4 preserved in payment_orphans\n  - status nulls = 0\n  - non-open statuses = 0\n  - created_at drift = 0\n  - payments with missing invoice = 0\n  - PRAGMA foreign_key_check returned no violations\n  - inserting a bad future payment failed with FOREIGN KEY constraint failed\n\n- after running migration a second time:\n  - invoices still = 3\n  - payments still = 3\n  - payment_orphans still = 1\n  - p4 still present exactly once\n  - no invalid payment references introduced\n\n- after rollback:\n  - invoices columns restored to old shape\n  - payments columns restored to old shape\n  - invoice rows = 3\n  - payment rows = 4\n  - p4 restored to payments\n  - payment_orphans table removed\n\nIf you want, I can also paste the final SQL contents inline.\n",
